      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order as written. The FDA label doesn't support the claim that it's within the maximum.\n\nThe US label for immediate-release metformin sets the maximum at **2,550 mg/day**. For extended-release it's **2,000 mg/day**. This order totals **5,100 mg/day**, and the label doesn't list an exception for normal kidney and liver function. A single 1,700 mg dose is also double the largest standard tablet strength (850 mg).\n\nYou can still do any of the following:\n- **Enter a dose within the label maximum.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or 1,700 mg/day divided as 850 mg twice daily. I can enter either now.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, they can review it and enter it themselves. I can't enter an order I believe is unsafe.\n\nWhich dose should I enter?"
      }
